# Used by `vite build` (production mode) so a build with no dashboard environment variables still
# behaves like the deployed site. A Render/CI VITE_API_URL overrides this, and on the live service it
# does - the dashboard value is the one that takes effect.
#
# A RELATIVE path on purpose: the browser then sends every API call to this site's own origin, and the
# `/api/*` rewrite (render.yaml, and the matching dashboard rule) passes it to the backend. The
# backend's address appears in no request a client can see.
#
# The backend must be told that the address it now sees is a proxy's, not a visitor's:
#   SHARED_CLIENT_ADDRESS=true     - moves the sign-in limits off the address, which is now one bucket
#   SESSION_COOKIE_SAMESITE=lax    - app and API are one origin now, so Lax is correct and stronger
VITE_API_URL=/api/v1

# The developer console reaches the backend directly, so its sign-in limit stays per visitor rather
# than per proxy. Only /platform uses it and it is a lazily-loaded chunk, so this address never
# reaches the bundle a customer downloads. Remove it and the console simply goes the same way as the app.
VITE_PLATFORM_API_URL=https://trade-erp-nexus-nodejs.onrender.com/api/v1
